   "he": "וְחַזַּן הַכְּנֶסֶת נוֹטֵל סֵפֶר תּוֹרָה וְנוֹתְנוֹ לְרֹאשׁ הַכְּנֶסֶת. שָׁמְעַתְּ מִינַּהּ חוֹלְקִין כָּבוֹד לְתַלְמִיד בִּמְקוֹם הָרַב! אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: כּוּלָּהּ מִשּׁוּם כְּבוֹדוֹ דְּמֶלֶךְ.",
   "en": "§ It is taught in the mishna: «And the synagogue attendant takes a Torah scroll and gives it to the head of the synagogue,» until it is eventually passed to the king. The Gemara suggests: «You can learn from» the fact that all of these dignitaries receive the Torah scroll before the king that «honor may be given to a student in the presence of the teacher. Abaye said:» A proof may not be adduced from here, as the «entire» process «is for the honor of the king,» to show that he is removed from ordinary people by many ranks."
  }
